Q: 1/4=138
R: hornpipe
S: Paddy Murphy
D: In Good Hands
Z: Daniel Bradbury
Z: abc-edited-by: Adlai Waksman
% simplified from concertina double-stops and ornaments
% added chords; see https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=w7Cpdxuf6ZI
N: From Kirsten:
N: There's no shortage of commentaries or versions ... 
N: https://thesession.org/tunes/5080
N: https://www.irishtune.info/tune/3732/ mentioned that the traditional repeat pattern
N: for the dance is  AABABA because the dance is 96 bars long.
N: I also learned from playing for Ceilis that you add an extra A to begin the dance 
N: (3 A's feels like a lot of A's :| )
K: Dmaj
